MVP: Canada USDC Wallet + Withdraw to Canada + USDC Receive
One sentence

A compliant Canada-based wallet that lets users fund with CAD, convert to USDC, receive USDC, and cash out to CAD—fast.

Target users for MVP
Canadian Nigerians / diaspora who already move money / hold USD value

Freelancers in Canada who receive USDC (or want USD exposure)

Businesses in Canada paying contractors internationally (later)

Core flows (MVP v1)

1) On-ramp

User e-Transfers / bill pay / EFT → CAD balance

Convert CAD → USDC (in-app)

2) Off-ramp

Convert USDC → CAD

Withdraw to Canadian bank account (EFT)

3) Receive

Give the user a USDC deposit address (custodial or segregated, your choice)

User receives USDC from anywhere (with screening/monitoring)

Why this is the correct MVP?

Fast to build vs card issuing + merchant acquiring
Revenue early: spread + fees on conversions/withdrawals
Proof of demand: deposits, repeats, retention
Proof of moat: can you run compliant rails cleanly + reliably?

MVP Scope: exactly what to build
Must-haves

KYC onboarding + sanctions/PEP screening

Basic risk rules (limits, velocity checks, country restrictions)

CAD funding method (start with e-Transfer or EFT depending on partner)

CAD↔USDC conversion

USDC receive address + transaction history

Withdraw to CAD bank

Customer support + dispute workflow

Statements/receipts (surprisingly important for trust)

Nice-to-haves (still MVP-friendly)

“Lock USD value” view (show USDC as “Digital USD”)

Savings “vault” (purely UI at first)

Transparent fees page + live quote

Do NOT build in MVP

Card issuance

Merchant checkout

Nigeria merchant acceptance

Full crypto multi-asset support

Multiple chains (start with one: likely Ethereum L2 like Base/Arbitrum, depending on partner)

Monetization (MVP)

Keep it simple:
Conversion spread (CAD↔USDC)
Withdrawal fee (flat or tiered)
optional: subscription for higher limits / faster settlement

MVP success metrics (what “traction” looks like)
% users who fund within 7 days
average deposits per user/month
repeat conversion rate (second conversion within 30 days)
average revenue per user/month
compliance metrics: fraud rate, suspicious activity rate, chargeback exposure (should be near-zero if we avoid cards early)